    ($SATQ$c17d9ba9$SATQ$, $SATQ$f74b2e01-3db6-4f1e-ab96-71e8146de67d$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$4330be35-52c5-47ed-be1c-da32b6c6f267$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.E.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear inequalities in one or two variables$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A number <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is at most <math alttext="17"><mn>17</mn>
</math> less than <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math> times the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>. If the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math>, what is the greatest possible value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["-2"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["-2"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="negative 2"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn>
</math>. It's given that a number <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is at most <math alttext="17"><mn>17</mn>
</math> less than <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math> times the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="x less than or equals 5 y minus 17"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn></math>. Substituting <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> in this inequality yields <math alttext="x less than or equals 5 left parenthesis 3 right parenthesis minus 17"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="x less than or equals negative 2"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>. Thus, if the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math>, the greatest possible value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="negative 2"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"c17d9ba9","external_id":"f74b2e01-3db6-4f1e-ab96-71e8146de67d","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"4330be35-52c5-47ed-be1c-da32b6c6f267","uId":"751897b0-c43c-44b7-b3f5-64f44ef61063","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.E.","skill_desc":"Linear inequalities in one or two variables","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A number <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is at most <math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math> less than <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math> times the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>. If the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math>, what is the greatest possible value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["-2"],"correct_answer":["-2"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"negative 2\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn>\n</math>. It's given that a number <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is at most <math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math> less than <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math> times the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x less than or equals 5 y minus 17\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> in this inequality yields <math alttext=\"x less than or equals 5 left parenthesis 3 right parenthesis minus 17\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x less than or equals negative 2\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>. Thus, if the value of <math alttext=\"y