ar sign 60.00\"><mo>$</mo><mn>60.00</mn></math> gift card to pay for movies online. He uses his gift card to buy <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> movies for <math alttext=\"dollar sign 7.50\"><mo>$</mo><mn>7.50</mn></math> each. If he spends the rest of his gift card balance on renting movies for <math alttext=\"dollar sign 1.50\"><mo>$</mo><mn>1.50</mn></math> each, how many movies can Henry rent?</p>","externalid":"151077e0-2b11-4c07-bc61-40cb9fc124a8","templateid":"812280c0-17e8-49fd-9381-df5aca5f9436","vaultid":"2cd1d44a-27b4-452e-97c8-f336bacb64c0","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"925655ab-e6e6-47b8-b9c1-b1a973bcae1a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"cb45f19f-2fd4-4c51-92a5-9a2a6952d173","content":"<p><math alttext=\"25\"><mn>25</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"29467f49-05ec-4539-a8c2-b6595a05aa76","content":"<p><math alttext=\"35\"><mn>35</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"19062a4e-9cb1-4f53-b39d-5b1e5cf1a6bf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1691007959807,"updateDate":1691007959807}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959807, 1691007959807),
    ($SATQ$c39dbbdf$SATQ$, $SATQ$1ede31ff-90cd-4739-bd83-5ba88c2b02cb$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear equations in two variables$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Line <math alttext="r"><mi>r</mi>
</math> is defined by the equation <math alttext="4 x minus 9 y equals 3"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>4</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mrow>
			<mn>9</mn>
			<mi>y</mi>
		</mrow>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>3</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Line <math alttext="s"><mi>s</mi>
</math> is parallel to line <math alttext="r"><mi>r</mi>
</math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane. What is the slope of line <math alttext="s"><mi>s</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"c645c21b-016a-4cd7-8b00-e3d32f1187d0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"nine fourths\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"22c209fb-b1e8-4ccb-a063-d3041b4981b3","content":"<p><math alttext=\"four ninths\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t<mn>9</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9b22f9b7-fdfc-4052-92ed-a485ccc6e2bf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 4\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"70b6d05b-34a0-4203-8f25-28f4a722b83f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 9\"><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["22c209fb-b1e8-4ccb-a063-d3041b4981b3"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. It's given that line <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="s"><mi>s</mi></math> is parallel to line <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane. This means that the slope of line <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> is equal to the slope of line <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="s"><mi>s</mi></math>. Line <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> is defined by the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4 x minus 9 y equals 3"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. This equation can be written in slope-intercept form <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals m x plus b"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="m"><mi>m</mi></math> represents the slope of the line and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math> represents the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of the line. Subtracting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4 x"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math> from both sides of the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4 x minus 9 y equals 3"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="minus 9 y equals minus 4 x plus 3"><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 9"><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals four ninths x minus one third"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. Therefore, the slope of line <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="four ninths"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>. Since parallel lines have equal slopes, the slope of line <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="s"><mi>s</mi></math> is also <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="four ninths"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the reciprocal of the slope of line <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="s"><mi>s</mi></math>, not the slope of line <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="s"><mi>s</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"c39dbbdf","external_id":"1ede31ff-90cd-4739-bd83-5ba88c2b02cb","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"b7805af3-3ccd-4741-a4e0-a8b8b126f1a4","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.C.","skill_desc":"Linear equations in two variables","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Line <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math> is defined by the equation <math alttext=\"4 x minus 9 y equals 3\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>3</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Line <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math> is parallel to line <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane. What is the slope of line <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"c645c21b-016a-4cd7-8b00-e3d32f1187d0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"nine fourths\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"22c209fb-b1e8-4ccb-a063-d3041b4981b3","content":"<p><math alttext=\"four ninths\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t<mn>9</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9b22f9b7-fdfc-4052-92ed-a485ccc6e2bf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 4\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"70b6d05b-34a0-4203-8f25-28f4a722b83f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 9\"><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["22c209fb-b1e8-4ccb-a063-d3041b4981b3"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It's given that line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math> is parallel to line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane. This means that the slope of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> is equal to the slope of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math>. Line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> is defined by the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4 x minus 9 y equals 3\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. This equation can be written in slope-intercept form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals m x plus b\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi></math> represents the slope of the line and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> represents the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of the line. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4 x\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math> from both sides of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4 x minus 9 y equals 3\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"minus 9 y equals minus 4 x plus 3\"><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 9\"><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals four ninths x minus one third\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. Therefore, the slope of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"four ninths\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>. Since parallel lines have equal slopes, the slope of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math> is also <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"four ninths\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the reciprocal of the slope of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math>, not the slope of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.&nbsp;</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1755117017716,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"c39dbbdf","skill_cd":"H.C.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Linear equations in two variables","createDate":1755117017716,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":"","external_id":"1ede31ff-90cd-4739-bd83-5ba88c2b02cb","primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"b7805af3-3ccd-4741-a4e0-a8b8b126f1a4","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Line <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math> is defined by the equation <math alttext=\"4 x minus 9 y equals 3\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>3</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Line <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math> is parallel to line <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane. What is the slope of line <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math>?</p>","keys":["22c209fb-b1e8-4ccb-a063-d3041b4981b3"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"c645c21b-016a-4cd7-8b00-e3d32f1187d0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"nine fourths\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"22c209fb-b1e8-4ccb-a063-d3041b4981b3","content":"<p><math alttext=\"four ninths\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t<mn>9</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9b22f9b7-fdfc-4052-92ed-a485ccc6e2bf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 4\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"70b6d05b-34a0-4203-8f25-28f4a722b83f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 9\"><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It's given that line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math> is parallel to line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane. This means that the slope of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> is equal to the slope of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math>. Line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> is defined by the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4 x minus 9 y equals 3\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. This equation can be written in slope-intercept form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals m x plus b\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi></math> represents the slope of the line and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> represents the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of the line. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4 x\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math> from both sides of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4 x minus 9 y equals 3\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"minus 9 y equals minus 4 x plus 3\"><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 9\"><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals four ninths x minus one third\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. Therefore, the slope of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"four ninths\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>. Since parallel lines have equal slopes, the slope of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math> is also <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"four ninths\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the reciprocal of the slope of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math>, not the slope of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.&nbsp;</p>","externalid":"1ed