    ($SATQ$ca452900$SATQ$, $SATQ$f751d621-537a-4175-801e-a9a856b72c00$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear equations in two variables$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">What is the slope of the graph of <math alttext="y equals StartFraction 5 x Over 13 EndFraction minus 23"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mfrac>
				<mrow>
					<mn>5</mn>
					<mi>x</mi>
				</mrow>
				<mn>13</mn>
			</mfrac>
		</mrow>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>23</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane?</p>$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$[".3846","5/13"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$[".3846","5/13"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="five thirteenths"><mfrac>
<mn>5</mn>
<mn>13</mn>
</mfrac>
</math>. The graph of a line in the <em>xy</em>-plane can be represented by the equation <math alttext="y equals m x plus b"><mrow>
<mi>y</mi>
<mo>=</mo>
<mrow>
<mrow>
<mi>m</mi>
<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
<mo>+</mo>
<mi>b</mi>
</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>, where <math alttext="m"><mi>m</mi>
</math> is the slope of the line and <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> is the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept. The given equation can be written as <math alttext="y equals left parenthesis five thirteenths right parenthesis x minus 23"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>23</mn></math>. Therefore, the slope of the graph of this equation in the <em>xy</em>-plane is <math alttext="five thirteenths"><mfrac>
<mn>5</mn>
<mn>13</mn>
</mfrac>
</math>. Note that 5/13, .3846, 0.385, and 0.384 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"ca452900","external_id":"f751d621-537a-4175-801e-a9a856b72c00","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"b7cebbde-3b6d-46af-a671-f5a5fec2de34","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.C.","skill_desc":"Linear equations in two variables","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">What is the slope of the graph of <math alttext=\"y equals StartFraction 5 x Over 13 EndFraction minus 23\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t\t<mn>13</mn>\n\t\t\t</mfrac>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>23</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane?</p>","answerOptions":null,"keys":[".3846","5/13"],"correct_answer":[".3846","5/13"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"five thirteenths\"><mfrac>\n<mn>5</mn>\n<mn>13</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math>. The graph of a line in the <em>xy</em>-plane can be represented by the equation <math alttext=\"y equals m x plus b\"><mrow>\n<mi>y</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>m</mi>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mi>b</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math> is the slope of the line and <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept. The given equation can be written as <math alttext=\"y equals left parenthesis five thirteenths right parenthesis x minus 23\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>23</mn></math>. Therefore, the slope of the graph of this equation in the <em>xy</em>-plane is